WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.483
A forward deployed engineer works close to the
people who bear the consequences of a system.

00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:11.398
The responsibility extends from understanding
an ambiguous request to helping the operation

00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:13.153
adopt a useful change.

00:00:13.223 --> 00:00:15.229
Technical work remains essential.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:21.144
The difference is the boundary of ownership: a
deployed feature is an intermediate milestone.

00:00:21.214 --> 00:00:27.657
An outcome requires observable workflow change,
a responsible operator, and evidence collected

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.007
after adoption.

00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:34.239
Keep these boundaries visible when stakeholders
celebrate a successful demonstration.

00:00:34.309 --> 00:00:37.211
Northstar Support asks for an AI assistant.

00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:40.971
Twenty agents handle access,
billing, and incident tickets.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:46.119
A polished demo receives applause, but
agents still copy tickets into a spreadsheet.

00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:51.117
The deployer has delivered software while
the operating workflow remains unchanged.

00:00:51.187 --> 00:00:55.965
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:56.035 --> 00:01:01.433
Write one statement describing the delivery
milestone and another describing the operating

00:01:01.503 --> 00:01:03.828
outcome. Name who could verify each.

00:01:03.898 --> 00:01:09.445
Delivery: the authorized reviewer can load
a ticket and inspect a routing suggestion.

00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:15.019
Outcome: agents use that suggestion in their
actual queue, with lower review time and no

00:01:15.089 --> 00:01:16.646
increase in misrouting.

00:01:16.716 --> 00:01:19.340
The engineering lead verifies delivery.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.461
Maya, the support lead, owns adoption evidence.

00:01:22.531 --> 00:01:28.504
A screenshot supports the first statement; a
defined observation period and review records

00:01:28.574 --> 00:01:29.875
support the second.

00:01:29.945 --> 00:01:32.761
Which evidence best supports an adopted outcome?

00:01:32.831 --> 00:01:34.815
A. A successful demo B.

00:01:34.885 --> 00:01:38.512
Observed workflow use and
predefined outcome measures C.

00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:40.225
A completed code review.

00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:41.767
The best answer is B.

00:01:41.837 --> 00:01:45.847
A demo and a code review show
intermediate delivery evidence.

00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:49.117
Adoption requires behavior
and operating measures.
